  "notes": "No official cause code was provided in FORM-366 fields (TBD/provisional). Narrative describes two physically distinct damaged components (motor; hub/blade assembly) both requiring replacement, modeled as separate FailureMode nodes both leading to fan inoperability. Systems described purely in 'System Design'/'Safety Analysis' context (e.g., portable emergency ventilation fan 3HVR-FN18 contingency, Auxiliary Building general ventilation dampers) were treated as design context and not modeled as System/Component nodes, per rule 6. SLCRS is explicitly stated to have been maintained in service (opposite train of ABFS maintained in service) providing continued filtered release capability, so treated as an operable backup. Previous occurrences section states no similar events occurred in the past three years at this plant -- no stub LER emitted since no specific prior LER is referenced."
